{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp1", "text": "Intention is the leader of things; intention is first, they’re made by intention. If with corrupt intent you speak or act, suffering follows you, like a wheel, the ox’s foot.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp1", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 30, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp3", "text": "“They abused me, they hit me! They beat me, they robbed me!” For those who bear such a grudge, hatred is never laid to rest.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp3", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp4", "text": "“They abused me, they hit me! They beat me, they robbed me!” For those who bear no such grudge, hatred is laid to rest.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp4", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp5", "text": "For never is hatred laid to rest by hate, it’s laid to rest by love: this is an ancient teaching.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp5", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 20, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp15", "text": "Here they grieve, hereafter they grieve, an evildoer grieves in both places. They grieve and fret, seeing their own corrupt deeds.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp15", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp20", "text": "Little though they may recite scripture, if they live in line with the teaching, having given up greed, hate, and delusion, with deep understanding and heart well freed, not grasping to this life or the next, they share in the blessings of the ascetic life.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp20", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 45, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp119", "text": "Even the wicked see good things, so long as their wickedness has not ripened. But as soon as that wickedness ripens, then the wicked see wicked things.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp119", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 27, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp120", "text": "Even the good see wicked things, so long as their goodness has not ripened. But as soon as that goodness ripens, then the good see good things.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp120", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 27, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp121", "text": "Think not lightly of evil, that it won’t come back to you. The pot is filled with water falling drop by drop; the fool is filled with wickedness piled up bit by bit.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp121", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 33, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp125", "text": "Whoever wrongs a man who has done no wrong, a pure man who has not a blemish, the evil backfires on the fool, like fine dust thrown upwind.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp125", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 28, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp127", "text": "Not in midair, nor mid-ocean, nor hiding in a mountain cleft; you’ll find no place on the planet to escape your wicked deeds.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp127", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp129", "text": "All tremble at the rod, all fear death. Treating others like oneself, neither kill nor incite to kill.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp129", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp130", "text": "All tremble at the rod, all love life. Treating others like oneself, neither kill nor incite to kill.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp130", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp136", "text": "The fool does not understand the evil that they do. But because of those deeds, that simpleton is tormented as if burnt by fire.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp136", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "harsh", "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "wrath", "selection": "tone in ['harsh', 'stern'] (curation, not generation)"}
